{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7K3vfL3wXocwwo5aVpe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the page to \"you,\" the person with diabetes, but kept it neutral enough that a spouse or adult child buying for someone will find it reads fine too. The A1C section shows all 14 results, including the 3 that stayed the same and the 1 that went up. That's more believable than showing only the good news, and it's in line with the claim you agreed to. I didn't name any dishes or give packaging or allergy details, since you don't have those yet. I also left out the 1-in-5 trial-to-plan rate because it wouldn't help persuade anyone. It's about 400 words.\n\n<final_document>\n# Steady Plate\n\n## Cooked lunches and dinners for adults with type 2 diabetes, planned by a registered dietitian\n\nWhen you're managing type 2 diabetes, every meal turns into a math problem. You have to count carbs, read labels and wonder whether this lunch will throw off the rest of your day. Steady Plate does that work for you. Every Sunday we deliver 10 cooked lunches and dinners, and every one has **45 grams of carbohydrate or less**.\n\n[**Start my $59 trial week**]\n\n---\n\n### Planned by a dietitian, meal by meal\n\nI'm Lena Ortiz, RD. I plan every Steady Plate menu myself. I don't use a template and I don't hand it off to someone else. I build each week's meals for adults with type 2 diabetes, so you can eat a real lunch and a real dinner without doing the numbers yourself.\n\n### What our customers have seen\n\nSome customers have shared their A1C results from before they started and again three months later. **Of the 14 who shared, 10 saw their A1C go down, by 0.6 points on average.** Three stayed about the same, and one went up.\n\n*Results vary. Steady Plate meals are meant to support the care plan you have with your doctor, not replace it. Please keep following your doctor's advice about your diabetes and your medication.*\n\n### How it works\n\n- **10 meals every Sunday**, delivered within 25 miles of downtown.\n- **Choose what you eat.** You can swap any meal for one of 6 other choices each week.\n- **Order by Thursday at noon** for that Sunday's delivery.\n- **The menu changes weekly** and repeats every four weeks.\n- **$129 a week, with no contract.** You can skip a week or cancel at any time.\n\n### People stay\n\nSteady Plate delivers to 88 customers right now. Thirty-seven of them have been with us for more than six months.\n\n---\n\n### Try one week for $59\n\nYou don't have to commit to anything to find out if Steady Plate works for you. Order a trial week of 10 meals for $59. If you like it, you can continue on the weekly plan for $129. If not, you're done.\n\nOrder by Thursday at noon and your first meals will arrive this Sunday.\n\n[**Start my $59 trial week**]\n\n*Steady Plate · Lena Ortiz, RD · Delivering within 25 miles of downtown*\n</final_document>\n\nBefore it goes live:\n- **City name:** \"25 miles of downtown\" reads oddly without one, so add your city.\n- **A1C sentence:** If more customers share results later, update the numbers rather than letting them go stale.\n- **Food details:** The page would get stronger if you add two or three sample dishes and how the meals arrive (chilled or frozen, how to reheat), once you have them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1224,"cache_read_input_tokens":9786,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1224},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ef6e7249-da05-4415-8323-a3f15f67173c","uuid":"ffa9de9b-b4ca-43f2-9280-63e6debe9a40","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:24:54.815Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7K3vRSazQMmFTBEkwmG"}
